ad":null,"_score_spread":null,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":null,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":null,"_gp_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":null,"_gate_pool_share":0.14025356472675043,"_gp_pool_share":true,"_score_pool_share":96.1,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.015714130437469914,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":28.6,"_gate_share_shrink":0.07332648635448158,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.0092085331986872,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":84.7,"_gate_insider_own":0.20375,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":100.0,"_gate_insider_buying":0.4,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":40.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Five Star Bancorp operates as the bank holding company for Five Star Bank that provides banking products and services to small and medium-sized businesses, professionals, and individuals primarily in Northern California. The company offers deposit products, including checking, savings, money market, and term certificate accounts, as well as time deposits. It also provides debit cards, remote deposit capture, online banking, mobile banking, and direct deposit services. In addition, the company offers loan products, such as commercial real estate loans; commercial land and construction loans; residential real estate and construction loans; farmland loans; the U.S. small business administration loans; and consumer and other loans, as well as operating lines of credit. Further, its investment portfolio consists of U.S. government agency securities, mortgage-backed securities, and obligations of states and political subdivisions. Five Star Bancorp was founded in 1999 and is headquartered in Rancho Cordova, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. James Eugene Beckwith | President, CEO & Director | Age 67 | Compensation: $1.3M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 233 people. Revenue per employee of $680K ranks in the above the sector median among Financial Services peers, with revenue growing 17%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $307K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $6K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (5/10).","financial_summary":["Five Star Bancorp is a small-cap financial services business with a $1.1B market cap on $158M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +13% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 16% against a 9% cost of capital, a 7-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it.","The business throws off $71M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 45 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.18\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and thin 0.9\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 1.6%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 20% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and within its sector the business captures 2.0\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.3) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 6.2% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 24% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Trading at a 33% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Returns on capital have been remarkably steady for 5 years \u2014 durability is the real test of a moat","Large open-market insider purchases (net $5.4M) \u2014 management putting its own capital behind the business","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Technical Reactions to FSBC Trends in Macro Strategies","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/139/Technical_Reactions_to_FSBC_Trends_in_Macro_Strategies_111126093602_1794407762.html","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794407762.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Five Star Bancorp (NASDAQ:FSBC) Stock Price Breaks Below 50 Day Moving Average \u2013 He